NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000402 "=head1 HOMEPAGE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000403 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000404 "Please visit the project's homepage at L<https://metacpan.org/release/Data-Sah-Filter>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000405 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000406 "=head1 SOURCE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000407 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000408 "Source repository is at L<https://github.com/perlancar/perl-Data-Sah-Filter>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000409 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000410 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000411 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 "L<Data::Sah>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 "L<Data::Sah::FilterJS>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 "L<App::SahUtils>, including L<filter-with-sah> to conveniently test filter from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 "the command-line."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 "L<Data::Sah::Coerce>. Filtering works very similarly to coercion in the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "L<Data::Sah> framework (see l<Data::Sah::Coerce>) but is simpler and composited"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 "differently to form the final filtering code. Mainly, input data will be passed"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 "to all filtering expressions."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 ""
